window.FIGS=[{"id":"fig-swk-atomicity-fix","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-atomicity-fix.tex","caption":"Separate commits can leave orphaned writes. One immediate-mode transaction makes the three local writes atomic; no distributed compensation protocol is needed. [internal, OP-11]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":155,"page":65},{"id":"fig-swk-capability-permission","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-capability-permission.tex","caption":"Capability and permission are independent. The shaded case is possible but forbidden---the state a collapsed vocabulary cannot express. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":122,"page":39},{"id":"fig-swk-claim-lifecycle","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-claim-lifecycle.tex","caption":"The guarded claim lifecycle as a finite-state machine. Acquire is a single atomic insert against a SQLite uniqueness constraint; re-claim and release are idempotent; expiry moves a claim to expired , from which the next read lazily sweeps it back to free . There is no queued state: losing callers receive 409 Conflict and must manage their own backoff. [internal, alg:acquire]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":107,"page":31},{"id":"fig-swk-commitment-oracle","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-commitment-oracle.tex","caption":"Closure requires a supported evidence reference rechecked by the daemon. Free-text assertions leave the commitment open; scope policy, not the agent, supplies its deadline. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":138,"page":52},{"id":"fig-swk-consistency-model","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-consistency-model.tex","caption":"Overlapping requests receive one commit order: A claims, B loses, A releases, C claims. Theorem states the five assumptions this ordering requires. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":152,"page":63},{"id":"fig-swk-continuity-organs","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-continuity-organs.tex","caption":"The continuity chain as an evidence-support profile, computed from the chapter's own status grades. What checkpoint inherits from memory already drops from full to notes only; what the outcome ledger inherits from continuity drops again, to partial; identity and market inherit only that partial residue, not an independent grade of their own. Downstream confidence cannot exceed the weakest upstream link. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":142,"page":55},{"id":"fig-swk-controllability-quadrant","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-controllability-quadrant.tex","caption":"Prevention needs both control of the event and observation sufficient to evaluate its guard: the shaded cell. The partial-observation theorem gives the formal condition. Outside this cell, detection is not automatic; private, unreported state may remain invisible. [internal; schematic]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":135,"page":49},{"id":"fig-swk-delegation-chains","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-delegation-chains.tex","caption":"The designed coordination lineage must be carried inside each signed authorization hop. Authenticating its bytes does not establish semantic task equivalence.","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":119,"page":38},{"id":"fig-swk-durability-dramatization","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-durability-dramatization.tex","caption":"With OS and database/WAL state intact, restart recovers a process-crash commit; power loss can erase an unsynchronized commit. The five-millisecond interval is illustrative.","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":103,"page":29},{"id":"fig-swk-enforcement-layers","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-enforcement-layers.tex","caption":"Refusal is not compulsory mediation. Grades are source-reported, not an independent runtime audit.","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":160,"page":67},{"id":"fig-swk-fencing-epoch","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-fencing-epoch.tex","caption":"Reassignment advances the fencing epoch. When agent pauses past its 60s lease TTL, the kernel increments the epoch to 105 and reassigns src/auth/jwt.ts to . The downstream storage broker rejects 's late write bearing epoch 104 with 412 Precondition Failed , preventing silent corruption. [internal, Theorem ]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":109,"page":33},{"id":"fig-swk-i12-dependency","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-i12-dependency.tex","caption":"I7--I9 depend on authenticated identity at every write path. A legacy path that accepts self-asserted identity can bypass otherwise correct owner checks; I12 remains partial. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":161,"page":69},{"id":"fig-swk-idempotency-gap","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-idempotency-gap.tex","caption":"A missing receipt does not reveal whether the effect happened. Twelve local SQLite cases, not a Port Daddy test. Receiver deduplication here atomically retains the key, payload, effect and receipt; a sender-side key alone does not supply that contract. [Local fixture, receipt_gap_experiment.py .]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":116,"page":36},{"id":"fig-swk-marker-decay","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-marker-decay.tex","caption":"With a prune threshold of , raising decay retention from to delays pruning from tick 29 to tick 59. [internal; analytic]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":37},{"id":"fig-swk-op9-reclass","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-op9-reclass.tex","caption":"One threat-table row moves through the OP-9 reclassification. The move adds partial kernel-credential defense but leaves shared-kernel and sandbox surfaces in scope; it is not proof of impossibility. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":163,"page":71},{"id":"fig-swk-race-dramatization","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-race-dramatization.tex","caption":"Port race under the single-writer kernel. Two agents request port 7421 one millisecond apart. SQLite's single-writer serialization commits Claude's claim first (yielding 201 Created ); Codex's racing acquire hits the primary-key uniqueness constraint and catches an atomic 409 Conflict identifying the active holder, triggering a clean fallback to 7422. [internal, alg:acquire]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":110,"page":34},{"id":"fig-swk-recovery-pipeline","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-recovery-pipeline.tex","caption":"Three recovery mechanisms precede admission. A failed critical check blocks service. The dashed group marks separate mechanisms, not a completed shared recovery invariant.","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":105,"page":30},{"id":"fig-swk-reference-monitor","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-reference-monitor.tex","caption":"Pre-commit mediation prevents the forbidden state. A subscriber observes it afterward and can only halt or compensate. Uniqueness constraints and boot gates mediate; the current policy monitor subscribes. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":122,"page":40},{"id":"fig-swk-rehydration-pipeline","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-rehydration-pipeline.tex","caption":"Proposed replay restores recorded inputs and durable task state, not hidden model inference state. Completeness remains unestablished; OP-4 is not closed. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":143,"page":57},{"id":"fig-swk-single-writer","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-single-writer.tex","caption":"Both requests arrive before the first commit. The writer orders their records and replies after each commit. This sequence assumes one writer; it does not establish power-loss durability.","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":97,"page":25},{"id":"fig-swk-stack-map","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-stack-map.tex","caption":"Read upward from L0. Higher layers depend on the records beneath them, but introduce their own assumptions. The blue tick identifies this chapter. The dashed machine floor is a dependency, not a fifth layer.","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":91,"page":19},{"id":"fig-swk-taint-automaton","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-taint-automaton.tex","caption":"Reading a secret records taint; it is never refused. Afterward the policy blocks mediated network egress, while leaving uncontrollable events enabled. [internal, b3_controllability.py ]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":131,"page":45},{"id":"fig-swk-ticket-lock-delta","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-ticket-lock-delta.tex","caption":"The proposed ticket queue covers cooperative release, but expiry still bypasses it. Bounded waiting remains unproved until both paths consult the queue (). [internal]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":114,"page":35},{"id":"fig-swk-workunit-machine","src":"whitepaper/figures/fig-swk-workunit-machine.tex","caption":"Five guards protect the work-unit lifecycle. In the two-principal model, all 536 reachable states satisfy six invariants; removing any guard exposes the counterexample listed below. [internal, c0_workunit.py ]","imported":false,"ch":1,"chapters":[1],"shared":false,"bookPage":147,"page":59},{"id":"fig-anchor-alg-confusion","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-anchor-alg-confusion.tex","caption":"Aligned security traces hold the wire bytes constant and vary only the source of algorithm authority. Header selection reaches acceptance without a signature check; issuer pinning forces Ed25519 and rejects the same tampered token. [verified, v1_refined.pv]","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":191,"page":92},{"id":"fig-anchor-capability-attenuation","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-anchor-capability-attenuation.tex","caption":"Every hop checks a rights subset and an expiry bound. A child may inherit its parent’s expiry when a longer lifetime is requested; it may never gain a new right.","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":189,"page":90},{"id":"fig-anchor-card-lifecycle","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-anchor-card-lifecycle.tex","caption":"A UML state machine gives one card ID exactly two guarded terminal exits. Fresh issuance is shown separately, with no outgoing path from the revoked or expired card. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":200,"page":98},{"id":"fig-anchor-cuckoo-inline","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-anchor-cuckoo-inline.tex","caption":"Bitwise OR corrupts stored fingerprints; set union preserves the identifiers needed to rebuild them. Two-bucket example with one three-bit slot per bucket.","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":195,"page":95},{"id":"fig-anchor-delegation-inline","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-anchor-delegation-inline.tex","caption":"Each signature binds adjacent identities, a nonce, and the task hash. Moving a legitimate signature to another hop fails because its signed identities and nonce no longer match. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":194,"page":93},{"id":"fig-anchor-four-phases","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-anchor-four-phases.tex","caption":"Each phase adds a check without removing earlier checks. The marked transition closes the named threat; later phases preserve that closure. [internal, Table ]","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":187,"page":94},{"id":"fig-anchor-handshake-ladder","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-anchor-handshake-ladder.tex","caption":"The issue--delegate--verify ceremony as a sequence diagram. Every message after m1 falls inside the shaded region, where the Daemon is not addressed: agent A mints card_1 from card_0 with its own key, and the Harbor accepts the chain under pk_daemon with no round trip to the issuer. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":193,"page":100},{"id":"fig-anchor-revocation-gossip","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-anchor-revocation-gossip.tex","caption":"The issuing daemon stops a revoked card locally. A remote verifier can still accept while its revocation update is undelivered; gossip convergence is not a global kill switch.","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":197,"page":97},{"id":"fig-anchor-v6v7-escalation","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-anchor-v6v7-escalation.tex","caption":"Checking only against the root misses re-escalation after an intermediate restriction. v7 checks each immediate parent and rejects the same chain that v6 admits. [internal; ProVerif multihop models]","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":231,"page":104},{"id":"fig-anchor-verification-stack","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-anchor-verification-stack.tex","caption":"Obligations descend from model to source to binary; tool evidence returns upward. The two correspondence gaps still require human justification. [internal, Table ]","imported":false,"ch":2,"chapters":[2],"shared":false,"bookPage":203,"page":102},{"id":"fig-sealed-composition-crossover","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-sealed-composition-crossover.tex","caption":"Analytical comparison for per-release and a fixed maximum horizon; queries may adapt. At , basic is 3.20 versus advanced 3.31. Advanced first has lower at , but allows ; basic keeps . Lower epsilon therefore trades guarantees, not uniformly stronger privacy.","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":144},{"id":"fig-sealed-controllability-quadrant","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-sealed-controllability-quadrant.tex","caption":"Room events on controllability witnessing. Complete mediation makes the upper-left cell invalid: every gate-controlled event is witnessed. The compound rule watches the read, then vetoes net_egress . [internal, b3_controllability.py ]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":265,"page":140},{"id":"fig-sealed-dual-attestation","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-sealed-dual-attestation.tex","caption":"One evidence bundle, two independent appraisals. Derek and Erin each release a key only after their own appraisal succeeds. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":249,"page":129},{"id":"fig-sealed-laundering-fork","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-sealed-laundering-fork.tex","caption":"The gate is unchanged; the worker changes its argument and reveals a distinction the original parity release hid. This arithmetic example is outside C1's committed-input model. [internal; Exercise ]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":263,"page":139},{"id":"fig-sealed-leakage-ledger","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-sealed-leakage-ledger.tex","caption":"For 200 jobs, fixed status plus three return slots yields about 13,117 bits of adversarial capacity. The capacity ledger accounts for both explicit payloads and discrete timing horizons without conflating their channels. [hand-derived; Exercise ]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":279,"page":152},{"id":"fig-sealed-mutant-grid","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-sealed-mutant-grid.tex","caption":"Both atomicity mutants break balance immediately. Only the torn write breaches the budget cap, after three steps in this two-client model. The intact model's 15 reachable states satisfy both invariants. [internal, a3_epsilon_ledger.py ]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":271,"page":143},{"id":"fig-sealed-operating-curve","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-sealed-operating-curve.tex","caption":"Three carried canaries give 99.2% conditional detection at . The stopping-time comparison uses , , , ; reported capped simulation means have no supplied uncertainty and do not certify error control.","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":277,"page":147},{"id":"fig-sealed-pillar-pipeline","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-sealed-pillar-pipeline.tex","caption":"Each owner authorizes removal of their own restriction. Dashed links bind controls to the signed work order; solid arrows carry outputs. Proposed control flow; public receipt omitted.","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":255,"page":134},{"id":"fig-sealed-receipt-provenance","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-sealed-receipt-provenance.tex","caption":"Hashes and the signature bind the recorded work order, evidence, inputs, model, policy state, and released ciphertext. The receipt proves what was reported, not that the output is true.","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":252,"page":131},{"id":"fig-sealed-residuals-converge","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-sealed-residuals-converge.tex","caption":"Alternative worker-chosen uses share one specified output envelope, not three allowances. The account prices that envelope before timing; is not bits, and the bound does not cover unmodeled host side channels. [internal, ]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":278,"page":150},{"id":"fig-sealed-three-principals","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-sealed-three-principals.tex","caption":"The room must keep Erin's model from Derek, Derek's data from Erin, and both from the cloud operator. One mechanism must satisfy all three separations. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":242,"page":125},{"id":"fig-sealed-two-adversaries","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-sealed-two-adversaries.tex","caption":"The same ledger conserves declared spend, not semantic privacy. DP needs valid mechanisms and complete mediation; bounds only the specified output channel before timing. [internal, ]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":270,"page":141},{"id":"fig-sealed-two-worlds","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-sealed-two-worlds.tex","caption":"Parity hides the difference between secrets 0 and 2; a raw-secret release exposes it. Reported model check: four secrets, depth 7, not unbounded executions. [internal, c1_noninterference.py ]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":261,"page":137},{"id":"fig-sealed-work-order-schema","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-sealed-work-order-schema.tex","caption":"The work order binds measurements, permitted execution, recipients, limits, and remedies. Hashes identify attested measurements, not live query-time state. Any field change requires both principals to sign again. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":3,"chapters":[3],"shared":false,"bookPage":248,"page":127},{"id":"legible-swarm-completion-verifier","src":"whitepaper/figures/legible-swarm-completion-verifier.tex","caption":"Vision: a proposed authority-side rule, not implemented enforcement or a guarantee of universal correctness. Passing it still leaves any omitted requirement unchecked.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":319,"page":176},{"id":"legible-swarm-consent-lifecycle","src":"whitepaper/figures/legible-swarm-consent-lifecycle.tex","caption":"Vision. Permission is not execution, and an action decision does not renew the grant.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":302,"page":164},{"id":"legible-swarm-escalation-band","src":"whitepaper/figures/legible-swarm-escalation-band.tex","caption":"For the R3 constants, no dismissal debit meets both constraints below . At , the feasible interval is . An empty band requires more capacity or better evidence. [verified, b7_escalation_band.py ]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":323,"page":178},{"id":"legible-swarm-hayek-scott","src":"whitepaper/figures/legible-swarm-hayek-scott.tex","caption":"Scott and Hayek offer complementary cautions: administrative legibility can erase local knowledge. Scott's later work suggests preserving the spaces where practical knowledge develops. [interpretive synthesis]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":374,"page":215},{"id":"legible-swarm-inception-canary","src":"whitepaper/figures/legible-swarm-inception-canary.tex","caption":"A sandbox replay tests whether the operator catches a known defect. Missing it tightens the autonomy grant; rejecting it widens the grant. The probe cannot alter production. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":331,"page":184},{"id":"legible-swarm-rate-regime","src":"whitepaper/figures/legible-swarm-rate-regime.tex","caption":"At , the positive-rate wedge lies between and ; the zero-rate boundary enters at and continues above-left outside the panel.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":191},{"id":"legible-swarm-readpoverty","src":"whitepaper/figures/legible-swarm-readpoverty.tex","caption":"Separate readers may each open eight items; the joint reader may open eight total. The comparison changes the total opening allowance. These counting lower bounds are not achieved implementation costs.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":339,"page":187},{"id":"legible-swarm-roles","src":"whitepaper/figures/legible-swarm-roles.tex","caption":"The operator grants once; the daemon gates or escalates each subsequent act. Operator override bypasses agents. A live fleet repeats the act-and-check pair, not the grant. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":373,"page":211},{"id":"legible-swarm-sa-levels","src":"whitepaper/figures/legible-swarm-sa-levels.tex","caption":"A read surface can expose evidence without establishing the operator's situation awareness.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":329,"page":182},{"id":"legible-swarm-sdt","src":"whitepaper/figures/legible-swarm-sdt.tex","caption":"Lowering the inspection threshold trades missed dangers for false alarms. The curves are idealized fixed Gaussians, not a fitted detector; the cost assumptions determine the preferred threshold. [internal, Definition ]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":326,"page":180},{"id":"legible-swarm-specialization","src":"whitepaper/figures/legible-swarm-specialization.tex","caption":"At three agents, pooling wins below and sole ownership above it. The dashed, superseded threshold diverges incorrectly; the worked point narrowly favours sole ownership. [internal; closed form]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":175},{"id":"legible-swarm-split-penalty","src":"whitepaper/figures/legible-swarm-split-penalty.tex","caption":"With opens in total, the joint floor exceeds the sum of two single-reader floors allowing opens each. These finite slices compare lower bounds, not achieved costs.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":365,"page":206},{"id":"legible-swarm-split-ranker","src":"whitepaper/figures/legible-swarm-split-ranker.tex","caption":"One pair crosses when Mira and the router disagree. Panel (a) shows concordant preferences (one ranking satisfies both readers); panel (b) shows the strict reversal where high irreversible risk inverts the top choices. Panels compare alternative objective preferences, not time.","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":352,"page":200},{"id":"legible-swarm-state-of-nature","src":"whitepaper/figures/legible-swarm-state-of-nature.tex","caption":"Three worked traces start from one settings.json revision. A keywise merge is benign; a raw splice fails immediately; a valid exclusion stays green until release replay exposes the hidden fixture. [internal, pedagogical counterexample]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":294,"page":160},{"id":"legible-swarm-zoom-advantage","src":"whitepaper/figures/legible-swarm-zoom-advantage.tex","caption":"Adaptive halving guarantees an advantage when . At , its guarantee is ; the harness mean is , distinct from that worst-case bound. [internal, zoom_bound_check.py ]","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":195},{"id":"legible-swarm-zoom-vs-potemkin","src":"whitepaper/figures/legible-swarm-zoom-vs-potemkin.tex","caption":"Two claim trees of identical shape. Top: the legible digest's three named claims each resolve to one artifact --- a diff, a test run, a review comment. Bottom: a same-shaped summary whose three claims resolve to nothing an operator can open. A safe summary is an index into evidence; a calm one that terminates early is a Potemkin digest, whichever claim count it advertises [internal].","imported":false,"ch":4,"chapters":[4],"shared":false,"bookPage":306,"page":167},{"id":"fig-stp-audit-amortization","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-stp-audit-amortization.tex","caption":"Model A's audit rate falls, but its cumulative bill has no finite ceiling. [verified, b2_tower.py , seed 20260816]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":465,"page":272},{"id":"fig-stp-dependency-spine","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-stp-dependency-spine.tex","caption":"Each lower capability requires the structural foundation beneath it; none follows from them alone. The ladder exposes the sharp boundary where the reference system's implemented reality stops today on the path to an operational market. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":399,"page":234},{"id":"fig-stp-deterrence-regime","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-stp-deterrence-regime.tex","caption":"Deterrence requires . For , the threshold is ; lower audit probability makes capture profitable. [internal; closed form]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":273},{"id":"fig-stp-engine-swap-regime","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-stp-engine-swap-regime.tex","caption":"Attestation changes which price can deter substitution; it does not guarantee the price gap. Analytic example: , , , (Theorem ).","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":442,"page":256},{"id":"fig-stp-handoff-coverage","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-stp-handoff-coverage.tex","caption":"An intact selection can omit a required instruction. Synthetic old fixture, handoff-coverage experiment of 20 September 2026, run 03; source functions tested with scanners stubbed. No provider behaviour or source recovery was tested.","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":423,"page":246},{"id":"fig-stp-judge-market","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-stp-judge-market.tex","caption":"Before selection, exclusions and a public draw support neutrality. After selection, a bond and later re-audit support accountability. Both stages leave checkable evidence. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":455,"page":267},{"id":"fig-stp-multidim-reputation","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-stp-multidim-reputation.tex","caption":"A favours accuracy and aesthetics; B favours efficiency. Different buyer priorities legitimately reverse the ranking. A universal average would erase that choice. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":453,"page":265},{"id":"fig-stp-nomint-lineage","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-stp-nomint-lineage.tex","caption":"Transfer spends each source balance; an undebited copy retains it. The first row counts inherited priors, the others spendable balances.","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":415,"page":241},{"id":"fig-stp-parfit-chain","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-stp-parfit-chain.tex","caption":"Parfitian continuity is an overlap chain, not permanent connectedness. Incarnation 1 shares witnessed outcome with incarnation 2; incarnation 2 shares with incarnation 3. No later body must directly remember : the overlapping evidence establishes the transitive ledger rail . The dashed counterexample repeats a label without a shared witness and therefore inherits nothing. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":410,"page":239},{"id":"fig-stp-probation-cliff","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-stp-probation-cliff.tex","caption":"At , delaying equal deterrence raises the newcomer's burden by . Front-loading is undominated; 4,000 searched instances found no improvement. [internal, b6_probation.py , seed 20260816]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":251},{"id":"fig-stp-rate-the-raters","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-stp-rate-the-raters.tex","caption":"In this parameterized example, eight cliques reach the honest-root boundary near level 27; one clique needs roughly 53. The bound assumes an honest root---it does not create one. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":461,"page":270},{"id":"fig-stp-resurrection-soundness","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-stp-resurrection-soundness.tex","caption":"A migration accepts only with principal-scoped sanctions, a continuity witness, engine-attested outcomes, and closed or escrowed obligations. The successor receives a continuing record, not a clean slate. [internal; schematic]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":444,"page":259},{"id":"fig-stp-role-vs-person","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-stp-role-vs-person.tex","caption":"A role stays while its occupants change. A person's witnessed record stays while bodies and roles change. Reputation belongs to that continuing identity, not the slot. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":406,"page":236},{"id":"fig-stp-sybil-whitewash","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-stp-sybil-whitewash.tex","caption":"Binding identity to a principal preserves sanctions across restarts and prevents aliases from multiplying quorum weight. This protection is local to one trusted domain, not cross-operator attestation. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":436,"page":253},{"id":"fig-stp-tombstone","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-stp-tombstone.tex","caption":"A tombstone removes a fraudulent contribution from future scoring without erasing history. Importing harbors remain exposed until it arrives; measures that convergence interval. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":5,"chapters":[5],"shared":false,"bookPage":469,"page":276},{"id":"fig-he-assurance","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-he-assurance.tex","caption":"In this analytic model, more independent reviewers reduce miss probability; perfectly shared outcomes do not. The lower panel is reserved budget, not realized payout.","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":547,"page":330},{"id":"fig-he-cold-start","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-he-cold-start.tex","caption":"Supplier pricing follows realized liquidity, not calendar time. Charging begins only above ; a market that never crosses the threshold never enters that regime. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":530,"page":318},{"id":"fig-he-conflict-kinds","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-he-conflict-kinds.tex","caption":"A policy can contain several conflicts: these counts are not disjoint shares. Synthetic sweep of policies, seed ; b4_deontic_fragment.py .","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":509,"page":304},{"id":"fig-he-conflict-witness","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-he-conflict-witness.tex","caption":"One Horn inference derives prod_access , activating overlapping obligation and prohibition intervals. Skipping propagation misses 100 of 885 conflicting sweep instances. [verified, b4_deontic_fragment.py ]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":511,"page":306},{"id":"fig-he-conservation-functor","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-he-conservation-functor.tex","caption":"Within , the illustrated wallet, escrow, and commons deltas sum to zero. A conversion records its rate, time, recipient amount, fee, and the execution shortfall relative to its quote; later rate movement remains an open exposure. [internal; illustrative values]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":516,"page":309},{"id":"fig-he-deontic-frontier","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-he-deontic-frontier.tex","caption":"Conflict checking is polynomial in the stated fragment; disjunctive obligations permit an NP-complete conflict-freedom problem. [verified, b4_deontic_fragment.py ]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":507,"page":302},{"id":"fig-he-deterrence-convention","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-he-deterrence-convention.tex","caption":"Same , , ; different forfeiture. Keep-gain takes , requiring audit rate . Claw-back takes , requiring . [analytic example]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":332},{"id":"fig-he-float-plan","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-he-float-plan.tex","caption":"Proposed admission order: requester bounty and provider bond are reserved together. The worker waits for the reservation receipt. The signed ceremony and enforced gate are not yet complete. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":500,"page":299},{"id":"fig-he-ms-wedge","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-he-ms-wedge.tex","caption":"Independent uniform values and costs on ,cr are an illustrative prior, not market data. The marked rental offers ,cr of surplus, below this equilibrium's ,cr trade threshold.","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":311},{"id":"fig-he-rater-ladder","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-he-rater-ladder.tex","caption":"Each appeal lowers a natural-number rank and stops at rank zero. That endpoint may be a protected oracle or a named final authority; termination does not turn preferences into objective truth. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":756,"page":325},{"id":"fig-he-skill-lineage","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-he-skill-lineage.tex","caption":"A versioned skill document binds v2 to its v1 parent while retaining a separate v2 evaluation root. The displayed counts illustrate a predeclared discounted prior, not evidence that v2 behaves like v1. [internal; illustrative]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":750,"page":322},{"id":"fig-he-succession-price","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-he-succession-price.tex","caption":"Chosen rates: task/h, /h and /h. The limiting floor exceeds the pool's h-equivalent cost, so increased skill alone cannot win here. Analytic model, not measurements.","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":314},{"id":"fig-he-three-sided","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-he-three-sided.tex","caption":"One refactor, three alternative purchases. Rental and licensing are designed, not shipped; all three use the same escrow. [illustrative]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[6],"shared":false,"bookPage":494,"page":294},{"id":"tab-keystone-split","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/tab-keystone-split.tex","caption":"The keystone split. Everything Alice's daemon knows about itself is also checkable from Bob's foreign view except the last row: a signed, intact history still does not prove who controls the foreign key. Log integrity crosses the trust boundary; accountable-principal binding does not, and that missing row is the stone the market rests on and does not yet have. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":6,"chapters":[5,6],"shared":true,"bookPage":447,"page":262},{"id":"fig-bc-delta-threshold","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-bc-delta-threshold.tex","caption":"Three-round punishment caps the loss; grim punishment does not. The curves assume shared, correct observations. The square is the archived four-round TLC counterexample, not a measured payoff series.","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":595,"page":388},{"id":"fig-bonded-cartel-folk-theorem-tikz","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-bonded-cartel-folk-theorem-tikz.tex","caption":"S means the cartel sustains; C means it collapses. Every simulated boundary lies within one tested grid step of the closed-form threshold (). Each configuration uses 5 , 000 trials, 200 rounds, and three colluders. [verified, proofs/bonded/pareto/simulation-cartel.mjs ]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":609,"page":378},{"id":"fig-bonded-conservation-ledger","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-bonded-conservation-ledger.tex","caption":"Only top-up increases supply. A partial breach moves from to : the full escrow closes, while total supply stays 10. [internal, Conservation.tla ]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":619,"page":385},{"id":"fig-bonded-inclusion-check","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-bonded-inclusion-check.tex","caption":"Two sibling hashes connect receipt to a four-record tree. Accept only when a trusted-key signature verifies and the roots match. The proof establishes inclusion, not truth.","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":576,"page":360},{"id":"fig-bonded-isolation-ladder","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-bonded-isolation-ladder.tex","caption":"The three isolation tiers order strictly by strength, weakest to strongest: none, advisory, structural. (advisory) is the default --- file claims are registered and reported but never block. Moving up buys more safety at the cost of parallelism; the choice between and specifically is not a security decision but an economics one, argued in Section 5. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":571,"page":352},{"id":"fig-bonded-key-custody","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-bonded-key-custody.tex","caption":"Each attack requires different access. These conditions exclude same-user code execution on the daemon host. [design invariant]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":626,"page":390},{"id":"fig-bonded-merkle-forest","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-bonded-merkle-forest.tex","caption":"Two inclusion paths connect a note to a signed root. Here, the hashes and signature occupy 736 bytes. [hand-derived]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":575,"page":358},{"id":"fig-bonded-regiment-boundary","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-bonded-regiment-boundary.tex","caption":"The transaction can prevent violations of its three local invariants. Checks requiring outside information belong to later detection and recovery. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":573,"page":354},{"id":"fig-bonded-session-lifecycle","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-bonded-session-lifecycle.tex","caption":"A crashed session becomes abandoned after the reaping threshold, then is salvaged or dismissed. File claims only inform; they do not exclude another claimant. [internal, BondedCommons.tla ]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":615,"page":382},{"id":"fig-bonded-sybil-deposit-floor-tikz","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-bonded-sybil-deposit-floor-tikz.tex","caption":"Reimbursing the commons does not eliminate attacker profit. Across the tested deposits, one or three Sybil identities remain profitable because slashing is capped by coverage. [verified, proofs/bonded/pareto/simulation-sybil.mjs ]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":607,"page":376},{"id":"fig-bonded-trust-collision","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-bonded-trust-collision.tex","caption":"Two uncoordinated agents edit and push the same file, ninety seconds apart. The second push conflicts; an invented resolution corrupts it. This is the chapter's opening scenario. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":350},{"id":"fig-cartel-game-inline","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-cartel-game-inline.tex","caption":"Cartel sustainability in the detection--loss plane. The curve marks : below it collusion pays; above it deviation pays. The two marked policies share the boundary, so detection frequency alone does not determine stability. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[6,7],"shared":true,"bookPage":608,"page":377},{"id":"fig-governance-flow","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-governance-flow.tex","caption":"Dispute resolution is an ordered four-stage escalation ladder. Each stage badge is keyed to the escalation trigger in the legend, and every stage outcome -- released, expired, preempted, or ruled -- discharges onto the same evidence rail regardless of which stage resolved the dispute. Escalation therefore changes only the decision cost and decision-maker, never the record kept for appeal. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":583,"page":356},{"id":"fig-magic-link-inline","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-magic-link-inline.tex","caption":"Overlapping requests still produce one consumption. A wins this illustrated schedule; either caller can win. SQL is simplified: authentication and expiry checks are omitted.","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":627,"page":391},{"id":"fig-pareto-dominance-tikz","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-pareto-dominance-tikz.tex","caption":"Competition's advantage over the static baseline depends on noise, collusion and insurer count: more insurers do not guarantee better outcomes. 2 , 000 trials per configuration, 50 transactions each; Wilson 95% intervals are within of the plotted rates. [verified, proofs/bonded/pareto/simulation.mjs ]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":606,"page":375},{"id":"fig-sen-pareto-locking","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-sen-pareto-locking.tex","caption":"Precautionary locks versus advisory claims. In panel (a), agent 's decisive lock on an unneeded file aborts agent 's task . In panel (b), advisory notification lets release , achieving the Pareto-superior outcome where both tasks succeed.","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":580,"page":365},{"id":"fig-sybil-inline","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-sybil-inline.tex","caption":"More identities multiply entry cost, not loss per default. Slashing stops at coverage ; deposits above that cap cannot increase the loss. Figure tests the resulting incentives. [internal, closed form]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":607,"page":375},{"id":"fig-worked-example","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-worked-example.tex","caption":"Three layers share one wall-clock axis. Process authority ends at minute 12 and a successor receives a new capability at minute 13. The evidence chain bridges the crash through a salvage-parent edge, while the pre-funded $6 escrow remains live until settlement at minute 24. The crash therefore disposes of identity without disposing of attribution or cleanup exposure. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":7,"chapters":[7],"shared":false,"bookPage":638,"page":400},{"id":"fig-fh-cochain-hand","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-fh-cochain-hand.tex","caption":"A visible loop exposes the lie ( ). Breaking even a different link lets the same lie pass with zero residual. Seeing the lying link alone is not enough. [verified, closed form; matches sheaf_consistency_radius.py ]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":null,"page":428},{"id":"fig-fh-conservation-ledger","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-fh-conservation-ledger.tex","caption":"Whole-bond status, not recipient balances. Clearance may divide the funds among payment, remainder, and fee. The status partition was model-checked for four harbors through depth 16; recipient conservation is a separate check. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":679,"page":432},{"id":"fig-fh-cycle-vs-cut","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-fh-cycle-vs-cut.tex","caption":"The same disagreement is detectable on the cycle ( ) but invisible on the path ( ). Detection requires a visible cycle. [verified, sheaf_consistency_radius.py ; seed 20260816]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":665,"page":424},{"id":"fig-fh-revocation-gossip","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-fh-revocation-gossip.tex","caption":"Revocation reaches each harbor separately: here refuses immediately, after , and after . A partition can extend staleness without bound. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[6,8],"shared":true,"bookPage":658,"page":419},{"id":"fig-fh-revocation-regime","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-fh-revocation-regime.tex","caption":"Expiry closes the window when operational guarantees are weaker. Without a partition bound, only expiry remains. The eight-round TTL is illustrative, not a measured deployment setting.","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":660,"page":420},{"id":"fig-fh-settle-protocol","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-fh-settle-protocol.tex","caption":"Posting a bond and announcing damage do not settle it. Escrow checks the proof against the signed conditions, then makes one terminal decision: clear or refuse. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":680,"page":434},{"id":"fig-fh-settlement","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-fh-settlement.tex","caption":"With a non-bypassable gate, recipient whitelist, and fee cap, custody closes only by payment or refund. Adding an operator-controlled escape exposes the entire balance, not merely the fee. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[6,8],"shared":true,"bookPage":676,"page":430},{"id":"fig-fh-sovereignty-fence","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-fh-sovereignty-fence.tex","caption":"Alice can issue a valid card; she cannot make Bob accept it. This refusal precedes the transfer ceremony. [illustrative]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":647,"page":412},{"id":"fig-fh-sponsor-lifecycle","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-fh-sponsor-lifecycle.tex","caption":"Probation ends in graduation or expulsion. Misconduct forfeits the sponsor's bond, giving the sponsor a reason to vet the newcomer before admission. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":683,"page":436},{"id":"fig-fh-threat-bands","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-fh-threat-bands.tex","caption":"Evidence differs by threat. Identity and replay have concrete artifacts; revocation and settlement depend on stated connectivity and custody assumptions. Admission, cartel monitoring, and centralization remain open. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[6,8],"shared":true,"bookPage":652,"page":415},{"id":"fig-fh-visible-topology","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-fh-visible-topology.tex","caption":"The auditor loses the DEF cycle, not its witnesses. DF remains visible but becomes a bridge. Illustrative topology: a surviving cycle does not itself establish a lie.","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":664,"page":422},{"id":"fig-fh-worked-example","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-fh-worked-example.tex","caption":"Beta's bound claim settles against Acme's bond. Revocation follows; the three-round estimate assumes reliable rounds, not a guaranteed deadline. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":684,"page":438},{"id":"fig-fh-xfer-ceremony","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/fig-fh-xfer-ceremony.tex","caption":"Only the offer and acknowledgement cross the boundary. The destination card has no more authority than the source card; then verifies locally. Later epoch roots carry revocation asynchronously. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[6,8],"shared":true,"bookPage":654,"page":416},{"id":"tab-fh-partition","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/tab-fh-partition.tex","caption":"Federation runs no consensus, so partition tolerance is decided protocol by protocol. Transfer stalls outright; revocation keeps working inside each side of the split; settlement holds its position until the split heals. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":692,"page":440},{"id":"tab-fh-revocation-rules","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/tab-fh-revocation-rules.tex","caption":"Three candidate revocation-conflict rules, evaluated against the same disagreement (harbor has revoked card ; harbor has not yet seen it). The adopted rule is the only one with a bounded attacker window under stated assumptions. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":662,"page":421},{"id":"tab-fh-sheaf-harness","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/tab-fh-sheaf-harness.tex","caption":"At seed 20260816, the named detection and silence gates pass. Across all arms, 313 of 1,101 residual detections are pairwise-blind. Supporting arms are not additional pre-registered gates. [verified, sheaf_harness_v2.py ]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":668,"page":426},{"id":"tab-fh-topology","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/tab-fh-topology.tex","caption":"Four rails connect sovereign harbors without a shared signing root. Witnessing authorizes nothing; settlement's custody bound depends on its gate being non-bypassable. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[6,8],"shared":true,"bookPage":null,"page":316},{"id":"tab-fh-witness-log","src":"website-v2/public/whitepaper/figures/tab-fh-witness-log.tex","caption":"Five witness-log properties, each closing a distinct federation failure. [internal]","imported":false,"ch":8,"chapters":[8],"shared":false,"bookPage":649,"page":414}];
